INTEGER and LONGINT arithmetic wraps on overflow.

The C backend used to emit signed C + - * and unary minus, whose
overflow is undefined behavior in C, so GCC folded x + 1 > x to TRUE
even at LAST(INTEGER).  It now does signed arithmetic in the unsigned
C type and casts back.  The LlvmIR backend emits add, sub and mul
without nsw/nuw flags.  Every line of output should be the same with
every backend and at every optimization level.
